<title>NETHERLANDS: Fortis confirms in talks over MeesPierson.</title>
<headline>Fortis confirms in talks over MeesPierson.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch-Belgian banking and insurance group Fortis confirmed on Thursday it was in talks with ABN AMRO bank over the purchase of its MeesPierson investment banking unit.</p>
<p>&quot;Fortis confirms it is in discussions with ABN AMRO bank at present over the possible acquisition of MeesPierson NV,&quot; the group said in a statement.</p>
<p>Spokesman Kees Leering added he could not comment on when a decision would be made.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO said on Tuesday it was in discussions after being approached by a number of parties interested in the unit, which analysts expect to be worth up to 2.5 billion guilders.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
